problem.cc (Changed on 4th June 2026, distributed assembly range):
Problem::parallel_sparse_assemble() called get_my_eqns(handler, el_lo, el_hi_plus_one - 1, ...).
el_hi_plus_one is unsigned and get_my_eqns() takes the INCLUSIVE upper index, so an empty
element range wrapped the subtraction to a huge number. This happens on a rank that ends up
with a single element. Guarded with "if (el_hi_plus_one > 0)".

problem.h (Changed on 25th May 2026, block dof arrangement):
